            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xxl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Unpleasant odors can make your home feel less comfortable, whether from cooking, pets, smoke, or everyday household activities. Many people wonder if air purifiers can actually remove these smells or just mask them temporarily.</p><p>The short answer is yes, air purifiers can remove smells and odors, but not all air purifiers are created equal. Success depends entirely on the type of filtration technology inside the unit. Understanding how your air purifier tackles odors will help you choose the right solution for your home.</p><h2>How Air Purifiers Remove Odors and Smells</h2><p>Air purifiers work by pulling air through a series of filters that trap particles and gases. While many people associate air purifiers with removing allergens like pollen and dust, odor removal requires a different approach.</p><p>Most odors are caused by volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and other gaseous molecules that float through the air. According to the <a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/indoor-air-quality-iaq/volatile-organic-compounds-impact-indoor-air-quality\">EPA</a>, VOC concentrations are consistently higher indoors than outdoors, often two to five times greater. Standard particle filters alone cannot capture these tiny gas molecules. A comprehensive systematic review of 148 field studies published in Science of the Total Environment found that air purifiers show very little effectiveness at reducing gaseous pollutants when relying solely on particle filtration, which is why activated carbon filtration becomes essential for odor removal.[1]</p><p>The key is activated carbon filtration. Activated carbon has been treated to create millions of microscopic pores, giving it an enormous surface area relative to its size. As air passes through your air purifier, odor-causing gases adhere to the carbon surface through a process called adsorption. The molecules stick to the carbon rather than passing back into your air.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-performance\">Blueair air purifiers combine HEPASilent™</a> technology with activated carbon filters to address both particles and odors simultaneously. HEPASilent™ technology captures 99.97% of airborne particles down to 0.1 microns while using minimal energy, making it an efficient solution for comprehensive air care.</p><h2>What Types of Household Odors Can Air Purifiers Remove?</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KnqYBR": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
